{# Light or dark, and nothing else.

   Two buttons rather than three. "Match system" was a third state and it is
   gone: it is the default rather than a choice, so it was a button that did
   what doing nothing already did. With no stored preference this file's media
   query follows the machine, and the control simply shows which way that came
   out -- so a reader on a laptop that dims at sunset still gets a dark page
   without ever pressing anything.

   `aria-pressed` and not `aria-current`: these are controls, not destinations.
   The markup ships with light pressed for everybody, because the same HTML
   goes to every reader and the choice is per-browser; the head script has
   already applied the real one and global.js corrects the buttons. #}
<div class="theme js-theme" role="group" aria-label="Colour theme">
    <button type="button" class="theme__option is-on" data-theme-choice="light" aria-pressed="true">
        <i class="fas fa-sun" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Light</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="theme__option" data-theme-choice="dark" aria-pressed="false">
        <i class="fas fa-moon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Dark</span>
    </button>
</div>
